{"availability":"available","full":"ayhankorkmaz/domat","name":"domat","description":"A Pomodoro timer with a task list on a tiny 3D farm. You focus, Grandpa Hasan grows the tomatoes. Three.js, no build step, offline, no tracking.","category":"Productivity","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-04T15:58:23Z","updated":"2026-10-10T20:02:39Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://getdomat.com","topics":["focus","offline-first","pomodoro","pomodoro-timer","productivity","pwa","task-manager","threejs","vanilla-js","webgl"],"demo":"https://getdomat.com/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:10.851Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:10.851Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:10.851Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:51:10.851Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Pomodoro timer with a task list, set on a tiny 3D farm.","Every focus session plants a seedling labeled with the task you're working on. On your break, the tomatoes are ready to pick.","If Domat helps you focus, a ⭐ helps other people find it."],"features":["Tasks with pomodoro estimates (1–10), tags, notes, drag-to-reorder, and daily or weekday repeats.","Each task shows its progress (2/4 🍅), and the list shows the whole day: 5 tasks · 9 pomodoros · done ≈ 7:15 PM.","The active task stays pinned to the timer. When its estimate runs out, Domat asks: done, or one more pomodoro?","Each seedling gets a small wooden sign with the task name and a ribbon in the tag's color.","Focus time by tag and by task, your most productive hours, a 12-month heatmap, streaks and an interruption count."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ayhankorkmaz/domat/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"11c4d672357e17ec699c789aa5e6a718e4daf4289f87a06290f0cfe43fde1970","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:10.996Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:10.996Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":